# NOTE (draft): the author list is still under review before release. Beata Myler
# and Victor Liu are added here per the shared genotyping author set. The Powell
# Lab / sceQTL-Gen legacy that much of this workflow is adapted from is credited
# in the `references:` block below (and in the abstract), which is the standard
# way to credit derived work -- rather than by listing its authors as authors of
# this repo. If the lab wants to list upstream contributors (e.g. Drew Neavin) as
# co-authors, that should be agreed with them first. version/date-released and the
# Zenodo DOI are added at release time.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this workflow, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "imputation: a genotype QC and 1000 Genomes imputation Snakemake workflow"
abstract: >-
  A Snakemake workflow that takes measured genotypes (VCF) and performs quality
  control (SNP filtering, sex and ancestry checks against a 1000 Genomes
  reference) and imputation of missing variants against a 1000 Genomes reference
  panel, followed by filtering to produce SNP profiles suitable for single-cell
  demultiplexing with Demuxafy. Much of the pipeline is adapted directly from the
  Powell Lab / sceQTL-Gen consortium imputation workflow (see references).
